   "html_text": "To address this problem, Shannon recovered and refined the concept of information, which other theorists such as Nyquist or Hartley had already used before: in Shannon’s characterization, the quantity of information at the source can be roughly understood as the amount of order (or, more precisely, its entropy). Intuitively, the amount of information reflects the uncertainty of the actual state of the source given all possible states in which it could be. Sources with many, equally likely states",
